From 8b8b4bda4933f5bd9fd1f64df2e3458dd9833e6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Francesco Stimola <francesco-stimola@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 21:40:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 16/18] nouveau: report the size of exported buffers

nouveau_screen_bo_get_handle never set whandle->size, so
vaExportSurfaceHandle gave every object a size of 0. GStreamer's VA
plugin warns about a driver bug for each plane of each surface and reads
the size from the fd instead.

Set it to the size of the buffer object.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_screen.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_screen.c b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_screen.c
index b144b89..f483f25 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_screen.c
@@ -145,6 +145,7 @@ nouveau_screen_bo_get_handle(struct pipe_screen *pscreen,
                              struct winsys_handle *whandle)
 {
    whandle->stride = stride;
+   whandle->size = bo->size;
 
    if (whandle->type == WINSYS_HANDLE_TYPE_SHARED) {
       return nouveau_bo_name_get(bo, &whandle->handle) == 0;
